```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .container {
            text-align: center;
            border: 2px solid #333;
            padding: 20px;
            width: 50%;
            background-color: white;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .button {
            cursor: pointer;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
            background-color: #007BFF;
            color: white;
            font-size: 16px;
            transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
        }
        .button:hover {
            background-color: #0056b3;
        }
        .joke {
            margin-top: 20px;
            font-style: italic;
            font-size: 18px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <p id="joke">[Funny Joke]</p>
        <button onclick="revealPunchline()" class="button">Push to reveal punchline</button>
        <div id="punchline" style="display:none;">
            <p class="joke">The punchline is here!</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline() {
            document.getElementById('punchline').style.display = 'block';
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple webpage with a container for the joke, a button to reveal the punchline, and some CSS styling to make it look more appealing
